  "summary": "Disconnect peers that send a sendtxrcncl P2P message after verack, regardless of whether -txreconciliation is enabled. Previously, nodes running with -txreconciliation disabled ignored post-verack sendtxrcncl messages instead of disconnecting the misbehaving peer.",
  "problem": "Nodes running with transaction reconciliation disabled do not enforce BIP 330 disconnection requirements when receiving a sendtxrcncl message after verack, violating the protocol specification.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'As mandated by BIP 330... always disconnect such a peer, regardless of the value of -txreconciliation. Previously the code would ignore and not disconnect such a peer if -txreconciliation=0.'"
